comments[3]:
  - created_at: "2026-10-29T22:37:33.033Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Duplicate check: hybrid linked-test search plus complete keyword only-last search returned completed selector execution/order lineage but no owner for selected-receipt verbosity; live open and in-progress lists checked; current issue report not yet reproduced on this source."
  - created_at: "2026-10-30T13:11:14.242Z"
    author: "harness:claude-code"
    text: "Implementation evidence: reproduced on the pre-fix build d9c4a0bca. A 4-test item's --only-last receipt printed all 4 tests[] rows, and the selection block was repeated as warning linked_test_selection:only-last=last;selected=1;skipped=3;indexes=4. projectTestResult now returns runSelection.selected as tests[] whenever a selector skipped at least one test. count keeps the full stored total, selection keeps the 1-based indexes and skipped count, and a new optional tests_omitted {count, restore_with: 'pm test <id> --list'} names the full-collection read. Unselected runs and --list are unchanged. The redundant selection warning is removed. Its only consumer was the unit assertion that is now replaced, and empty_linked_test_selection is untouched. Measured on a 58-test fleet-shaped item, --only-last: TOON 8662 to 2212 bytes (-74%), JSON 18826 to 2695 bytes (-86%), pre-fix build vs this build on the same tracker. The SDK runTest result and CLI --json are covered in test-command.spec.ts for match, only-index and only-last, plus --list restore and the unselected run. MCP pm_test forwards through the same runTest result. SDK surface acknowledged for the optional TestResult.tests_omitted. Follow-up observation, not in scope: the remaining ~1.2 KB of a selective receipt is mostly execution_context, which repeats sandbox paths even when no context mismatch occurred."
  - created_at: "2026-10-31T08:33:31.744Z"
    author: "harness:claude-code"
    text: "Review follow-up on PR #1635 (CodeRabbit full review of f86d1539e, 2026-10-31): the `tests_omitted.restore_with` command had three scope gaps.\n\n1. **Shell safety.** `--pm-path` was emitted bare or inside JSON double quotes, so a path such as `/tmp/$HOME` (or one containing backticks) would expand when copied into a shell. The command is now rendered by the shared `renderPmCommand` / `quoteCommandArg` helpers, which escape `$`, backticks, quotes and backslashes on POSIX and use CommandLineToArgvW quoting on Windows.\n2. **Extension scope.** A narrowed run under `--no-extensions` produced a restore command that re-enabled extensions. The receipt now carries `--no-extensions` when the invocation used it.\n3. **Tracker scope.** A tracker selected through `PM_PATH` has no `--path` flag, so the restore command omitted it and could read a different tracker in the next shell. `resolveLinkedTestRestoreScope` keeps the resolved root as `--pm-path` when `PM_PATH` selected it; a tracker found by discovery stays implicit.\n\n`renderTrackerPathFlag` is replaced by `renderLinkedTestRestoreCommand(itemId, scope)` plus `resolveLinkedTestRestoreScope(global, pmRoot)` in `src/sdk/test/execution-receipts.ts` (keeping `src/sdk/test/execution.ts` under the 3400-line cap). Evidence: `tests/unit/sdk/test/execution-receipts.spec.ts` (posix `$`/backtick escaping, win32 quoting, `--no-extensions`, PM_PATH vs discovery) and `tests/unit/commands/test/test-command.spec.ts`, which replays the emitted command and gets all three linked tests back.\n\nSecond review round: `docs/TESTING.md` now tells readers to copy and run the complete `tests_omitted.restore_with` command rather than a bare `pm test <item-id> --list`, which would drop `--pm-path` and `--no-extensions`. PowerShell expansion of `$(...)` and backticks inside win32 double quotes affects every rendered recovery command, not only this one, so it is tracked separately in pm-kjoudp instead of patched per call site.\n\nFourth review round: `resolveLinkedTestRestoreScope` now uses the same precedence as `resolvePmRoot`, so a blank `--path` falls through to `PM_PATH` instead of dropping the tracker from the restore command."
    edited_at: "2026-10-31T13:17:49.209Z"
